From: Santiago <villavicencioandrs@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] json: support empty arrays

Upstream json_parse_array() enters the value parsing loop immediately
after matching '[', without checking whether the array is empty. This
fails on empty arrays such as "sr_service": [] found in modemr.jsn,
causing pd-mapper to exit with code 1 before registering QRTR services.

Skip whitespace and check for ']' before entering the value loop,
returning success with an empty array if matched.
---
 json.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/json.c b/json.c
index 28834d8..e3e1174 100644
--- a/json.c
+++ b/json.c
@@ -196,6 +196,12 @@ static int json_parse_array(struct json_value *array)
 	}
 
 	array->type = JSON_TYPE_ARRAY;
+	json_skip_whitespace();
+	ch = input();
+	if (ch == ']')
+		return 1;
+	unput();
+
 	do {
 		value = calloc(1, sizeof(*value));
 		if (!value)
-- 
